    "created_at": "2022-02-24T19:27:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-24T19:27:18Z",
    "body": "> > On Apple platforms, there is no distinction between focus & selection. As such, we need to tie them together.\r\n> \r\n> This doesn't appear to be Apple platform-wide thing, but instead a choice Safari has made on Apple platforms. (The demo at https://bug1755215.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9263674 has separate selection and focus in Chrome on Apple platforms.)\r\n\r\nWell, I'm saying this is the underlying platform / operating system convention. Whether any specific UA follows that convention or not is up to each UA. Safari tries to match the OS / platform convention as much as it can.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
